WEBVTT

00:02.590 --> 00:04.220
You're so lucky, Nico!

00:04.600 --> 00:10.140
You keep saying "I was there for work,"
but you totally got to enjoy Okinawa!

00:10.390 --> 00:13.840
You know what? This sucks!
Don't you think so, Fuuri?

00:13.841 --> 00:18.405
SATA
ANDAAGI
DONUTS

00:18.406 --> 00:22.409
She brought back a ton of souvenir snacks, so I'm
pretty happy. Still, I don't see any sea grapes...

00:22.410 --> 00:26.870
Ah, I'm sorry! Uh, well, the thing is...

00:27.290 --> 00:31.420
A Red Tide Corps
monster stole them from me.

00:31.580 --> 00:33.539
Huh? What's that?

00:33.540 --> 00:37.590
I'm not sure I understand, but I bet
it was a lot of trouble, huh?

00:38.420 --> 00:39.669
Hey, you girls!

00:39.670 --> 00:43.090
The stage is free. It's a
little early, but you can use it.

00:43.300 --> 00:45.139
Thank you, Aako.

00:45.140 --> 00:46.679
Thank you very much.

00:46.680 --> 00:49.139
Okay, let's have a session!

00:49.140 --> 00:50.020
Yeah!

00:50.020 --> 00:51.020
Yesh!

00:52.270 --> 00:56.400
Fuuri? Only DRINKS are
allowed in the studio, okay?

00:58.030 --> 00:59.030
Regret!

01:02.360 --> 01:03.859
Ippai hibiki MUSIC
Ring out, tons of music

01:03.860 --> 01:05.369
Ippai kimari POSING
Do tons of cool posing

01:05.370 --> 01:06.869
Ippai todoke FEELING
Let tons of feelings reach you

01:06.870 --> 01:08.369
Super Soni let's go!
Super Soni let's go!

01:08.370 --> 01:09.829
Suggoi shigeki tenkomori
Stimulation super piling up

01:09.830 --> 01:11.346
Suggoi tama ni karamawari
Sometimes super running in circles

01:11.370 --> 01:12.959
Suggoi kimi to zutto ENJOY
Always super enjoy being with you

01:12.960 --> 01:15.210
Super Soni LET'S GO! Desu
Super Soni let's go! Yes

01:27.180 --> 01:31.640
Saikin omoitsukimashita
Lately, I've come to realize

01:33.270 --> 01:37.610
Kimochi tsutaeru tte taihen
That getting feelings across is tough

01:39.360 --> 01:44.149
Umaku dekitari dekinattari
Whether it goes well or not

01:44.150 --> 01:47.909
Muzukashii kara oku no te de
Is tough, so my trump card

01:47.910 --> 01:50.490
Mouretsu taiatari desu
Is going for it at full force

01:52.250 --> 01:54.540
Dakedo hitomishiri (hitomishiri)
But I'm shy (shy)

01:55.170 --> 01:57.970
Gomakashite senobi (senobi)
I act like it's nothing and aim high (high)

01:58.340 --> 01:59.879
Ashi ga gakuburu de
With legs trembling

01:59.880 --> 02:03.130
Hirakinaotte arinomama GO!
I get serious and just go for it!

02:03.510 --> 02:06.129
Zenkai, soukai, daitenkai Recuperation,
exhilaration, a big revolution

02:06.130 --> 02:09.180
Nandemo chokushin STRAIGHT
No matter what, keep heading straight

02:09.510 --> 02:12.179
Sekai, mankai, mugendai
The world, in full bloom, infinity

02:12.180 --> 02:15.729
Kyou mo genki ni koko ni imasu (HEY!) I'm
here again today, living to the fullest (Hey!)

02:15.730 --> 02:17.246
Ippai hibike MUSIC
Ring out, tons of music

02:17.270 --> 02:18.689
Ippai kimari POSING
Do tons of cool posing

02:18.690 --> 02:20.336
Ippai todoke FEELING?
Let tons of feelings reach you

02:20.360 --> 02:21.609
Super Soni let's go!
Super Soni let's go!

02:21.610 --> 02:23.279
Suggoi shigeki tenkomori
Stimulation super piling up

02:23.280 --> 02:24.609
Suggoi tama ni karamawari
Sometimes super running in circles

02:24.610 --> 02:26.426
Suggoi kimi to zutto ENJOY
Always super enjoy being with you

02:26.450 --> 02:28.620
SUPER SONI LET'S GO! Desu
Super Soni let's go! Yes

02:39.750 --> 02:41.129
Okay, finished!

02:41.130 --> 02:42.750
Thank you very much.

02:43.510 --> 02:45.300
Excellent work, Sonico.

02:45.670 --> 02:51.099
Thank you for everything, Mr. Manager.
Do you think the shoot went okay?

02:51.100 --> 02:57.440
Yes, no problems. And you were a big help,
bringing in your own guitar.

02:57.810 --> 03:01.610
The client didn't say they'd like to
have one in the shoot till the last minute.

03:01.860 --> 03:08.110
No problem at all! I'm sure being used for some
wonderful pictures makes my guitar happy, too.

03:08.530 --> 03:11.580
That guitar is quite
precious to you, isn't it?

03:13.990 --> 03:17.250
This guitar has a name: "Daydream."

03:17.410 --> 03:24.669
Ah, but it wasn't me who named it. It was an
alum from my music club back in middle school.

03:24.670 --> 03:26.970
You've had that since middle school?

03:27.220 --> 03:34.600
Yes. I inherited it from my upperclassman.
Still, maybe "inherited" isn't the best word...

03:35.020 --> 03:38.939
It was more like, I
wasn't able to return it.

03:38.940 --> 03:40.149
Something bad happened?

03:40.150 --> 03:45.190
Oh, no. I just lost touch with her.

03:51.490 --> 03:55.580
This guitar holds a lot of memories for me.

03:56.330 --> 03:59.150
PUB

03:57.160 --> 03:58.409
That was delicious!

03:58.410 --> 04:00.039
See you later, Leyla.

03:59.151 --> 04:01.970
ZEPPELIN

04:00.040 --> 04:01.960
And you too, Sonico!

04:02.210 --> 04:06.379
Thank you very much. Are you sure
you don't need umbrellas?

04:06.380 --> 04:10.679
No problem! "Let us be soaked by the
gentle showers of spring," right?

04:10.680 --> 04:11.220
Quotin' "Tsukigata Hanpeita" now?

04:11.220 --> 04:12.140
Note: "Tsukigata Hanpeita" is a 1952 samurai
film. Quotin' "Tsukigata Hanpeita" now?

04:12.141 --> 04:14.259
Note: "Tsukigata Hanpeita" is a 1952 samurai
film. "Oh, Master Tsuki! It's raining."

04:14.260 --> 04:14.390
Note: "Tsukigata Hanpeita" is a
1952 samurai film. Yeah, that's it!

04:14.391 --> 04:16.140
Yeah, that's it!

04:17.180 --> 04:20.689
Good work, Sonico. You must be tired.

04:20.690 --> 04:23.150
No. I'm fine, Grandma.

04:23.360 --> 04:26.150
Oh, that's right! I forgot.

04:26.610 --> 04:30.530
A postcard came, addressed to you.

04:30.900 --> 04:32.070
Here you go.

04:35.920 --> 04:37.539
Sonico
Doing well?
-TOMA

04:37.540 --> 04:38.770
Sonico

04:37.540 --> 04:40.000
-TOMA

04:38.771 --> 04:40.000
Doing well?

04:40.870 --> 04:45.960
There's no return address.
Is that a friend of yours?

04:47.050 --> 04:48.420
Sonico?

04:52.630 --> 04:57.510
I wonder what country that's from...
Are you doing well, Senpai?

04:58.770 --> 05:02.730
I'm sure you are, right?
Like, YEAH in the old days.

05:05.940 --> 05:10.280
I first met Tomano in my
second year of middle school.

05:11.650 --> 05:12.900
And like tonight...

05:13.490 --> 05:18.120
it was raining. A tender, fleeting, and...

05:18.630 --> 05:20.249
Daydream

05:20.250 --> 05:22.330
gentle rain.

05:23.920 --> 05:29.340
Back then, I'd fallen hard for rock, which
seemed like it could shake my soul to the core.

05:29.590 --> 05:33.380
I spent every free moment listening
to CDs of different bands.

05:34.130 --> 05:36.890
Being shy and an introvert to boot,

05:37.140 --> 05:41.685
I wanted to be passionate
forthright, like a rock musician.

05:41.686 --> 05:43.310
Daily Duty:
Super

05:44.850 --> 05:46.309
Ah. Um...

05:46.310 --> 05:47.310
Hm?

05:47.480 --> 05:49.190
What, Sonico?

05:49.690 --> 05:57.690
Uh, well... Y-your printout. Um, the
teacher said I should get it from you.

05:58.370 --> 06:05.000
Printout? Oh, sorry! I haven't done it yet.
Can you tell Teacher I'll turn it in tomorrow?

06:05.170 --> 06:09.709
Um, understood. I shall pass that along.

06:09.710 --> 06:17.390
I'm sorry! Also, Sonico, loosen up! We're
classmates, so you don't have to be so formal.

06:17.640 --> 06:20.509
Ah, Right! Understood.

06:20.510 --> 06:21.559
That's not much better.

06:21.560 --> 06:22.560
Aya!

06:23.350 --> 06:24.350
We're leaving.

06:24.560 --> 06:28.020
Okay, I'm coming. Well,
thanks again, Sonico.

06:28.270 --> 06:32.479
Ah! Yes. I will inform the teacher.

06:32.480 --> 06:33.609
Hey there.

06:33.610 --> 06:34.400
You took your time!

06:34.401 --> 06:35.569
Sorry 'bout that.
You took your time!

06:35.570 --> 06:37.660
C'mon, let's go.

06:40.950 --> 06:42.200
Okay!

06:42.210 --> 06:43.289
Staff Room

06:43.290 --> 06:46.120
All right. If you'll excuse me.

06:51.040 --> 06:52.040
It's raining...

06:55.880 --> 06:58.720
What should I do? I don't have an umbrella.

06:59.760 --> 07:01.180
And I rode my bike.

07:01.850 --> 07:05.680
Grandma's usually grocery
shopping around now...

07:16.490 --> 07:22.160
Oh. I know this song. It's
on one of Grandma's CDs.

07:29.840 --> 07:32.340
Music Room

07:44.350 --> 07:45.350
What?

07:46.430 --> 07:49.640
Uh, um... I just...

07:50.310 --> 07:52.150
Rain's got you stuck here, too?

07:52.400 --> 07:56.110
Um, that is... Yes. Uh...

07:56.820 --> 07:57.860
Wanna join me?

07:59.200 --> 08:05.120
You like rock, right? Why else would a middle
schooler walk over to the high-school wing to listen?

08:05.740 --> 08:08.500
What do you play? Guitar? Bass?

08:08.960 --> 08:14.209
Ah! Um, I... don't play any instruments.

08:14.210 --> 08:15.960
Can you sing, then?

08:17.460 --> 08:19.340
Do you know that song I was playing?

08:19.510 --> 08:25.049
Yeah. Um... Yes! It's
"M1oonlight Star" by Global Grave.

08:25.050 --> 08:26.050
Correct.

08:26.430 --> 08:27.430
Okay, sing.

08:28.350 --> 08:30.189
I-I can't!

08:30.190 --> 08:31.190
Why not?

08:31.770 --> 08:34.979
I know the song, but
the lyrics are in English!

08:34.980 --> 08:39.359
Just do what you can.
We're not performing in front of anyone.

08:39.360 --> 08:43.490
B-but... I'm embarrassed.

08:45.160 --> 08:48.239
How can you like rock
if you're gonna be shy?

08:48.240 --> 08:52.040
Rock is about expressing
yourself full force, right?

08:52.540 --> 08:53.879
Give it your all.

08:53.880 --> 08:57.130
Just be like, "YEAH," and sing it.

08:57.420 --> 09:00.220
Like, "Yeah," you say?

09:01.630 --> 09:02.630
Let's go!

09:09.020 --> 09:10.979
"Living simple, let your
heart lead the way—"

09:10.980 --> 09:13.380
Sing it louder! "Living simple,
let your heart lead the way—"

09:14.270 --> 09:15.310
SING IT!

09:19.280 --> 09:21.320
"Shoot down highway star"

09:21.490 --> 09:23.320
"So it's time to change"

09:24.320 --> 09:26.869
"Shout down, 'Walk this
way, ' so it's time to start..."

09:26.870 --> 09:29.510
Now scream! "Shout down, 'Walk
this way, ' so it's time to start..."

09:30.370 --> 09:31.540
Yeah!

09:31.960 --> 09:32.999
Again!

09:33.000 --> 09:34.710
YEAH!

09:35.750 --> 09:39.460
Top of the 15th, two outs, bases
loaded, No. 4 Ebikawa at bat.

09:39.710 --> 09:41.759
Pitcher Yanagigawa throws his first ball!

09:41.760 --> 09:42.510
A hit!

09:42.511 --> 09:44.380
Ah, but it's a wobbly grounder!

09:47.220 --> 09:48.640
I'm home!

09:49.510 --> 09:51.720
You're late, Sonico.

09:52.230 --> 09:56.100
I'm sorry. I waited out the rain at school.

09:56.770 --> 09:59.480
I'll get dinner ready for you.

09:59.900 --> 10:02.190
Okay. Thank you, Grandma.

10:03.860 --> 10:06.359
Did something good happen today?

10:06.360 --> 10:09.409
Wow! How did you know, Grandma?

10:09.410 --> 10:14.000
I can tell how my granddaughter feels.
So, what happened?

10:14.370 --> 10:18.330
Well, at school waiting for the rain
to stop, I met a high-schooler...

10:20.800 --> 10:23.210
I never asked her name.

10:26.630 --> 10:27.680
Must be nice.

10:28.340 --> 10:31.970
If I could play the guitar like that...

10:32.640 --> 10:33.980
I'm sure...

10:36.440 --> 10:37.440
I'm sure.

10:43.190 --> 10:44.610
Huh? No way!

10:44.990 --> 10:46.699
We can't cover that song.

10:46.700 --> 10:48.569
It's too hard, Toma!

10:48.570 --> 10:50.409
Come on, let's do it.

10:50.410 --> 10:52.119
Consider it a challenge.

10:52.120 --> 10:54.119
Easy for YOU to say, Toma.

10:54.120 --> 10:57.580
That's right. It's too
much for us to tackle!

10:58.830 --> 11:00.000
What are you doing?

11:04.590 --> 11:05.800
Wh-what?

11:06.090 --> 11:07.630
Um...

11:08.760 --> 11:16.060
Th-thanks very much for the other day.
My name is Super Sonico. U-um...

11:16.520 --> 11:20.480
I brought you s-some
snacks to thank you for before.

11:20.770 --> 11:22.480
I-if you'd like some...

11:24.900 --> 11:26.070
Come on in.

11:28.860 --> 11:30.530
You call inari sushi "snacks"?

11:30.780 --> 11:32.659
It should be chips or something, right?

11:32.660 --> 11:37.870
I-I'm sorry. I've really only made
traditional food before...

11:39.790 --> 11:40.960
It's delicious.

11:41.130 --> 11:43.170
Ah! Thank you very much!

11:43.630 --> 11:47.340
But you didn't come just
to give us "snacks," right?

11:49.050 --> 11:50.760
You have another reason.

11:51.140 --> 11:53.890
Um, well... Uh, that is...

11:54.260 --> 11:56.020
I, I...

11:56.810 --> 12:01.730
I want to learn the guitar, too!
Would you please let me join the band club?

12:02.360 --> 12:02.900
Sure.

12:03.150 --> 12:05.400
I'm sorry! It was selfish to...

12:05.780 --> 12:06.780
Huh?

12:06.900 --> 12:11.320
If you don't have a guitar,
I'll lend you mine. Welcome to the club.

12:11.570 --> 12:12.740
Uh, okay...

12:14.830 --> 12:17.289
Thank you very much!

12:17.290 --> 12:18.290
Sure.

12:18.710 --> 12:21.249
S-so then...

12:21.250 --> 12:21.830
What?

12:22.170 --> 12:25.420
Well, your name...

12:25.750 --> 12:30.550
I never told you? Kyoko
Tomano. Call me Toma.

12:31.130 --> 12:35.510
And so, that's how I joined the band club.

12:35.810 --> 12:40.730
It's how I learned to play guitar,
the rock that I loved so much.

12:54.040 --> 12:56.000
Music Room

13:00.540 --> 13:03.170
No, no good! It has to be more powerful.

13:03.670 --> 13:07.590
Put everything into it, DA-DA-DAAA!
SKREEE! Do it like that!

13:07.920 --> 13:13.340
Um, okay! DA-DA-DAAA! SKREEE! Right?

13:21.680 --> 13:24.060
Kokoro wa hitotsu
Our hearts are one

13:24.310 --> 13:29.690
Konna kirei na sora wa tsunagatteiru kara
This lovely sky joins them together

13:30.070 --> 13:33.910
Soba ni iru ki ga shita
So I've felt like you're at my side

13:34.700 --> 13:37.700
POCKET ni shinobaseta
I keep hidden in my pocket

13:40.620 --> 13:44.250
Kimi to no hibi dakishime The days
I've spent with you, and embrace them

13:46.250 --> 13:49.380
Torimodose MIGHTY HEART
Take back that mighty heart

13:49.630 --> 13:52.420
Kuchizusamu MELODY
Hum that melody

13:52.760 --> 13:59.100
Tomadoi sae ima yuuki ni kaete
You can turn even hesitation into courage

13:59.310 --> 14:02.140
Boku wa tsuyoku naru
I'll become strong

14:02.350 --> 14:05.519
Kimi o shinjiteru
I believe in you

14:05.520 --> 14:10.480
Sou sa, mou ichido kono te ni tsukamu
Yes, till the day I can grab you

14:10.780 --> 14:12.940
Sono hi made
With this hand once more

14:14.530 --> 14:16.319
You've gotten pretty good.

14:16.320 --> 14:19.660
That's impressive, getting so good
at the guitar in one year.

14:19.990 --> 14:24.790
Thank you very much. I have the support and
encouragement of you, my seniors, to thank for it.

14:25.080 --> 14:26.580
Man, you're so formal...

14:27.040 --> 14:29.420
Still, must be nice to
be a middle schooler.

14:30.550 --> 14:33.919
As a senior, you can automatically
transfer into the high-school division,

14:33.920 --> 14:35.680
so you'll have plenty
more time to practice.

14:36.550 --> 14:39.639
But my other two members are
studying for college entrance exams.

14:39.640 --> 14:41.430
They don't have time to practice.

14:41.810 --> 14:44.980
Are you going to college, Tomano?

14:45.230 --> 14:52.650
Me? I'm not sure. I don't like studying, but
I'm not good enough at the guitar to turn pro.

14:52.940 --> 14:56.990
That's not true! Your playing is wonderful!

14:58.700 --> 15:00.660
Thank you. Oh, that's right.

15:02.950 --> 15:04.999
I want you to have this guitar, Sonico.

15:05.000 --> 15:12.590
Huh?! I couldn't! It's so precious to you.
I-I couldn't take this! It's too much.

15:13.090 --> 15:14.090
This guitar...

15:14.670 --> 15:19.140
A graduate of the music club gave it to me.
And this is what he said:

15:19.840 --> 15:24.310
"I'm glad a girl like you, someone I
can entrust this to, joined the club."

15:25.270 --> 15:29.270
So, just like he chose
me, I choose YOU, Sonico.

15:29.730 --> 15:31.610
Miss Tomano...

15:31.810 --> 15:36.110
However! You can't have it just yet.
You need to get better.

15:36.490 --> 15:41.620
I know. I'll officially give it to you when
you can do a perfect cover of "Moonlight Star."

15:42.240 --> 15:45.289
"M-Moonlight Star"?

15:45.290 --> 15:46.409
But I can't!

15:46.410 --> 15:49.039
That song's too hard for me to play!

15:49.040 --> 15:52.920
It doesn't have to be right away.
Practice with all you've got.

15:53.340 --> 15:56.340
With that "Yeah" feeling of yours.

15:59.220 --> 16:03.430
I look forward to it. To you
playing "Moonlight Star."

16:04.890 --> 16:10.100
Why did Tomano suddenly
choose to give me her guitar?

16:10.690 --> 16:14.110
It would be another month
before I learned the reason...

16:14.440 --> 16:18.650
Almost exactly a year
since I'd joined the band club.

16:20.150 --> 16:22.370
T-Tomano is...

16:23.030 --> 16:24.370
transferring?

16:24.910 --> 16:27.200
'Cause of her parents, it looks like.

16:27.660 --> 16:28.830
Sorry, Sonico.

16:29.120 --> 16:31.830
We knew what was going on, but...

16:32.330 --> 16:36.129
She said she didn't want a
send-off or anything like that.

16:36.130 --> 16:37.250
No...

16:39.130 --> 16:41.549
So, when does she leave?

16:41.550 --> 16:43.389
Well, it's today.

16:43.390 --> 16:44.010
What?!

16:44.220 --> 16:50.480
Toma said to tell you only after she'd
transferred. We kind of jumped the gun.

16:51.190 --> 16:54.440
We already got to say our goodbyes to her.

16:55.610 --> 16:57.110
So, go right now.

16:58.570 --> 17:00.570
Okay... OKAY!

17:06.990 --> 17:08.449
No running in the halls!

17:08.450 --> 17:10.620
Sorry, sir! I didn't mean to!

17:15.130 --> 17:16.290
Tomano...

17:17.670 --> 17:18.670
Tomano!

17:20.090 --> 17:21.800
Kyoko, hurry up.

17:22.340 --> 17:23.380
Coming now.

17:26.010 --> 17:27.050
Sorry, Mom.

17:27.510 --> 17:29.020
Can I have a minute?

17:36.940 --> 17:38.610
Dammit, those two...

17:41.650 --> 17:44.860
Sorry. I hate teary goodbyes.

17:45.910 --> 17:47.450
I'm really sorry.

17:47.950 --> 17:52.830
I'm sorry, too, Tomano.
Here's your guitar back.

17:53.160 --> 17:59.840
I practiced so much, but...
I still can't play "Moonlight Star."

18:00.170 --> 18:05.050
I can't keep my promise to you. So then...

18:06.180 --> 18:12.140
You're so honest, Sonico.
But Daydream belongs to you now.

18:12.850 --> 18:14.599
"Daydream"?

18:14.600 --> 18:19.360
This guitar's name. The senior who
gave it to me named it.

18:20.320 --> 18:23.739
It's English for something you imagine,
or wishful thinking.

18:23.740 --> 18:30.159
I like that name a lot.
Fill this guitar with your dreams, Sonico.

18:30.160 --> 18:32.830
Then make those dreams real through rock.

18:33.750 --> 18:35.290
You can do it.

18:35.660 --> 18:39.840
But I... can't play "Moonlight Star."

18:40.250 --> 18:41.800
That's a dream, too.

18:42.630 --> 18:44.010
Make it come true.

18:45.050 --> 18:49.850
I won't come back to Japan for a while,
so will you play it for me when I do?

18:50.510 --> 18:54.600
Play "Moonlight Star" for me on Daydream.

18:55.350 --> 18:57.560
Tomano...!

19:02.650 --> 19:07.610
Ah, jeez. I knew this would happen. That's
why I wanted to leave under the radar.

19:08.030 --> 19:10.120
I swear. Sonico, you dope.

19:11.160 --> 19:14.660
I'm sorry! But... But...!

